                <pb facs="0438" n="320" sameAs="frus:frus1928v02/pg320"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">124.9318/128: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Perkins</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-09-13T12:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">September 13,
                                1928—noon</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>311. It is the desire of the War Department to have a report as to whether, from
                    the point of view of the Minister, the troops and agencies of the United States
                    Army in China have fulfilled the expectations of, and been satisfactory to, the
                    Department of State. It is requested that the Minister prepare and transmit such
                    a report, as soon as he returns from leave.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
